# The bundlers EMBED the engine modules into the generated bundle, so
# bundles/ also collects stale copies of gpu_port.py, numpy_port.py, ... .
# They are build output, not source: they are snapshots (the 2026-10-05 set
# was still sitting here) and they drift from the root modules by
# construction.  Only the make_*_bundle.py bundlers are source.
bundles/checkpoint_hub.py
bundles/distill.py
bundles/gpu_port.py
bundles/numpy_port.py
bundles/tail_credit.py
bundles/teacher_table.py
bundles/telemetry.py
bundles/train_gpu.py
# generated Colab bundles (colab_lrladder_*.py, colab_p0_gate.py, ...)
bundles/colab_lrladder_*.py
bundles/colab_p0_gate.py
# eval transcripts cached beside checkpoints (fs_verdict.py); regenerate with
cache/
bundles/__pycache__/
fs_corpus/
fs_*.npz
# generated Colab bundles. None of them embed a credential any more (the token
# is resolved at runtime), but they are machine-local and untracked regardless.
*.log
models/
*.npz
*.pid
*.pyc
__pycache__/
# the ruler (~10 min CPU each), so never commit them

# sha256 sidecars that checkpoint_hub.push writes next to a checkpoint;
# they outlive the .npz and were left orphaned by the repo cleanup
*.sha256

# experiment output (756 MB); keep history readable for rig commits
runs/
runs/lrroles/*.npz
